# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): the ways a vote ends (make_resolution, called by hand with the votes poked
# into the window's own table: 0x6ff6d4 is the vote of faction 0 and each faction's is 4 bytes on; -1 yea, -2 nay, a faction's number a vote
# for it). A proposal with a yea and a nay that fails on the nays (the result box says so, and the panel counts them); the election of a
# governor that ends in a tie (no one is elected); the governor elected again (the label that follows the name differs); the Supreme Leader
# proposal that gets a majority but not three fourths of the votes (it fails, and says what he would have been), the same with all
# in favour, which passes. The windows are closed by Escape, which carries the proposal out when it passed (the last one is not closed:
# a Supreme Leader's victory would end the game). The state regions are as in councwin_vote.scene.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
